# What must never reach a build context, and what simply has no business in an
# image. The first group is the security boundary: `docker build` sends the
# context to the daemon and every COPY layer is readable by anyone who can pull
# the image, so a `.env` excluded here is a `.env` that cannot leak
# (docs/ENGINEERING_STANDARDS.md §Security).

# --- Secrets and personal data ----------------------------------------------
# V1's real API credentials, and `.env.example` with them since the image needs
# neither: configuration arrives as environment variables from the composition.
.env
.env.*

# Job-board logins, browser sessions, the SQLite tracker, answers.yaml (name,
# address, date of birth). The importer reads the tracker through a read-only
# bind mount at /data instead — nothing is baked in.
data/

# The CV library and every rendered PDF carry full contact details.
cv/
cv_versions/
*.pdf

# The Excel tracker (folder name uses U+2019).
Rechercher d’emploi/

# Agent and IDE configuration, including local API keys.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/

# --- Not needed at runtime ---------------------------------------------------
# History, and a large context to send for nothing.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# A host virtualenv holds macOS binaries that cannot run in a Linux image, and
# copying it would shadow the site-packages `pip install -e .` creates.
.venv/

# Runs on the host and on CI against the exposed port, and the image installs no
# dev extras, so a copy here could not be executed anyway.
tests/

# --- Frontend dependencies and generated output ------------------------------
# docker/frontend.Dockerfile runs its own `npm ci`: the host node_modules holds
# macOS binaries (esbuild, rolldown, the Playwright browsers) that cannot execute
# in a Linux image, and copying it would shadow the install. Everything else here
# is generated — `.nuxt/` is rewritten by `nuxt prepare` on every build, and the
# Playwright output is a report about a run that happened somewhere else.
# `frontend/dist` is the symlink `nuxt generate` leaves behind: it points at an
# absolute host path that does not exist in the image.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.nuxt/
frontend/.output/
frontend/dist
frontend/.data/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/

# --- Caches and build output -------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.firecrawl/
.playwright-mcp/
out/

# --- OS noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
